  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixed a shared CFG005/CFG006 false negative found by evidence-based audit: struct- and record-struct-typed nested options properties were excluded from analysis because the nested-object gate filtered on TypeKind.Class only, even though the real ConfigurationBinder binds and recurses into struct properties. A typo under a struct-typed nested property went unflagged (CFG006) and a nested struct carrying validation attributes without recursive validation was skipped (CFG005). The gate now also accepts TypeKind.Struct (primitive and BCL value types stay excluded), and CFG002 consistently recurses into a [ValidateObjectMembers] struct property's members even when its section is absent, since a struct's default(T) is a non-null instance DataAnnotations validates at runtime. The generated appsettings.schema.json output is unchanged. Diagnostic IDs and severities are unchanged.",
